Fix XR FTBFS with deprecated=no (DISABLE_DEPRECATED).

XRInterface::get_projection_for_view() / get_transform_for_view() are
declared only under #ifndef DISABLE_DEPRECATED (servers/xr/xr_interface.h
and every interface subclass), but three callers/definitions were left
unguarded, so scons deprecated=no fails:

  modules/mobile_vr/mobile_vr_interface.cpp:676: 'get_projection_for_view'
    was not declared in this scope
  scene/3d/xr/xr_nodes.cpp:222,245,275,304: 'class XRInterface' has no
    member named 'get_projection_for_view'
  servers/xr/xr_interface_extension.cpp:243,249: definitions of members
    whose declarations are gated away

- mobile_vr: inline the projection math the deprecated wrapper uses
  (Projection::set_for_hmd with the interface's own lens parameters),
  minus its WARN_PRINT_ONCE and its side effect on `aspect`.
- xr_nodes: go through XRServer::get_camera_projections(), the modern
  path this same file already uses in _update_projections(); XRServer
  keeps the deprecated fallback itself, correctly gated.
- xr_interface_extension: gate the two definitions like their
  declarations.

Present in 4.8-dev6 and still in upstream master as of 2026-09-16;
no upstream PR found. Drop once upstream compiles with deprecated=no.

